BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T153000
UID:69d8176a1e64afd01e681c25@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Weston Branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variety o
 f trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry team to explore the natur
 al world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize different s
 pecies and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\nChil
 dren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nThe tour will st
 art and end at the Weston Branch and will be guided by the City of Toronto
  Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along the ro
 ute. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e.g. g
 loves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This progra
 m takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather\, re
 gistrants will be notified of an alternative date.\nThis program is part o
 f TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toro
 nto Public Library\, South Chapter.​\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
 tion can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397
 -5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Weston\, Youth Hub Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69d8176a1e64afd01e681c25
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Start & Grow Your Business with Enterprise Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T183000
UID:6a087391278f7c2f008d8a96@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Information session on how to start\, plan\, finance and grow 
 your very own small business.\nOwning a business is a dream for many peopl
 e. Every new business starts with an idea. This interactive presentation w
 ill give an overview of how to make it happen and the opportunity to ask q
 uestions related to your business. An advisor from Enterprise Toronto will
  present an overview of information related to the business planning proce
 ss\, evaluating a business idea\, financing\, marketing planning\, busines
 s structures\, regulatory requirements\, and more.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room1
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a087391278f7c2f008d8a96
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Branch Art Exhibit: Works by Natalia Ionescu
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260702T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T235959
UID:6a35437ff56bd86e00b7bfdc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Throughout the month of July\, works by artist Natalia Ionescu
  are on display at Agincourt Branch.\nNatalia is passionate about finding
  beauty and inspiration in all the people\, places and situations that she
  encounters in her everyday life. She loves sharing with others what th
 e world looks like through her lens in a way that might brighten up their 
 day\, and contributing to our community in a meaningful way.\nNatalia is a
 n immigrant artist from Eastern Europe who studied design there. She arriv
 ed to Canada as an adult and built a new life here together with her fami
 ly. She spent a few years in the social work field\, and is currently wor
 king in the corporate world.\nThis exhibit is part of TPL's\nArt Exhibits 
 Space\nprogram. Toronto Public Library provides space for local artists to
  exhibit their work at locations across the city. These exhibits aim to re
 flect the diverse cultural interests of the city and its neighbourhoods.\n
 The exhibit can be viewed during\nAgincourt\nbranch open hours.\nFree. All
  are welcome.\nImage credit: Natalia Ionescu\; watercolour and pencil\; "
 Canadian Spring"
LOCATION:Agincourt\, First floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a35437ff56bd86e00b7bfdc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
